From 5b1badb6000722c441c6a15077d121ed8476948c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:12:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 62/70] ppc32: answer maglev's CpuOperation::kMathClz32 query
 for the 32-bit target

Static finding while designing the ppc32 Maglev layer (no G5 cycle
yet).  14.6 added a second CpuOperation ladder to the Maglev graph
builder, kMathClz32, next to the kFloat64Round one that 0043 patched
at 12.4.  Like the first one it lists every backend and #errors for
anything else, and V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC (ppc32) is in no branch.  The
graph builder is one of the fifteen src/maglev TUs the harness
compiles even with V8_ENABLE_MAGLEV off (Turboshaft's
maglev-graph-building-phase reaches into it unconditionally,
BUILD.gn:5496), so this is a certain compile error for the delivered
series, independent of the Maglev switch.

Answer true: cntlzw is base PowerPC (G3/G4/G5 all have it) and the
ppc backend's MaglevAssembler::CountLeadingZerosInt32 is exactly
cntlzw, so Int32CountLeadingZeros is executable here once Maglev is
on.  The Float64 variant (Float64CountLeadingZeros) stays off because
the graph builder additionally gates it on kFloat64Round, which 0043
answers false for ppc32.  While Maglev codegen is off the answer is
only reachable through the Turbolev frontend (--turbolev, default
off), so it changes nothing in the current build posture.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 v8/src/maglev/maglev-graph-builder.cc | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/v8/src/maglev/maglev-graph-builder.cc b/v8/src/maglev/maglev-graph-builder.cc
index a531c45..06dd9e6 100644
--- a/v8/src/maglev/maglev-graph-builder.cc
+++ b/v8/src/maglev/maglev-graph-builder.cc
@@ -134,7 +134,9 @@ bool IsSupported(CpuOperation op) {
 
     case CpuOperation::kMathClz32:
 #if defined(V8_TARGET_ARCH_ARM64) || defined(V8_TARGET_ARCH_S390X) || \
-    defined(V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64)
+    defined(V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64) || defined(V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC)
+      // ppc32: cntlzw is base PowerPC (G3/G4/G5), see
+      // MaglevAssembler::CountLeadingZerosInt32.
       return true;
 #elif defined(V8_TARGET_ARCH_ARM)
       return CpuFeatures::IsSupported(ARMv8);
